1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,165
Can you show me docker build?

2
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:13,818
docker build turns a Dockerfile and a folder of files (the build context) into an image.

3
00:00:13,818 --> 00:00:17,921
The Docker CLI sends the context to the builder (BuildKit),

4
00:00:17,921 --> 00:00:21,953
the builder runs the Dockerfile's instructions one by one,

5
00:00:21,953 --> 00:00:27,446
and the result is stored as an image with the name and tag you give it with -t.

6
00:00:27,446 --> 00:00:30,088
This lesson covers the command itself:

7
00:00:30,088 --> 00:00:35,024
