37
00:02:45,328 --> 00:02:46,966
What is it, really?

38
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:51,697
The last argument of docker build is the build context:

39
00:02:51,697 --> 00:02:54,978
the folder whose files the builder may use.

40
00:02:54,978 --> 00:03:01,082
The CLI sends that folder to the builder (BuildKit) before any instruction runs,

41
00:03:01,082 --> 00:03:04,210
and COPY/ADD can only read files from it.

42
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:05,507
Two consequences:

43
00:03:05,507 --> 00:03:11,001
everything in the context is transferred (big folders make builds slow),

44
00:03:11,001 --> 00:03:18,250
and a Dockerfile can never copy a file from outside the context, such as ../shared/config.json.

