119
00:08:09,933 --> 00:08:12,258
Why would I need build layers?

120
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:17,077
Every RUN, COPY and ADD instruction produces a layer:

121
00:08:17,077 --> 00:08:21,354
the set of files that step added, changed or deleted.

122
00:08:21,354 --> 00:08:27,165
An image is its base image's layers plus one layer per such instruction,

123
00:08:27,165 --> 00:08:33,379
stacked; other instructions (WORKDIR, CMD, ENV, EXPOSE) only change metadata.

124
00:08:33,379 --> 00:08:35,074
Layers are immutable:

125
00:08:35,074 --> 00:08:40,885
a later step can hide a file, but never remove it from an earlier layer.

