144
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,735
What should I know about the build cache?

145
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:20,220
BuildKit remembers every layer it built.

146
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:26,280
Before running a step, it checks whether it has already built the same instruction,

147
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:30,588
on the same parent layer, with the same input files; if so,

148
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:34,385
it reuses the stored layer (CACHED) in milliseconds.

149
00:10:34,385 --> 00:10:40,080
As soon as one step changes, that step and every step after it must run again.

150
00:10:41,833 --> 00:10:45,793
